-- title:
--   Finiteness over K(t) for every transcendental t
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra satisfying the project's curve axioms `IsCurveOver K F`, namely: (i) every nonzero $f \in F$ admits a divisor $D$ on the places of $F/K$ whose value at each place $v$ is $v.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ and whose degree is $0$, where a place is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring; (ii) the residue field of every such place is a finite $K$-module; and (iii) the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega_{F/K}$ is free of rank one as an $F$-module. Assume in addition that $F$ is essentially of finite type over $K$ (`Algebra.EssFiniteType K F`). Then for every $t \in F$ transcendental over $K$, the field $F$ is finite-dimensional as a vector space over the intermediate field $K\langle t\rangle = K(t)$ generated by $t$. No perfectness or separability hypothesis on $K$ is imposed, and the characteristic is arbitrary.
--
--   This is the standard finiteness statement for one-variable function fields: $F$ is a finite extension of the rational subfield generated by any transcendental element. It is used throughout the curve theory of the project, for instance to compute the transcendence degree of $F$ over $K$ and in the local analysis of places and their fibres.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver_finiteDimensional_adjoin_simple_of_transcendental_of_essFiniteType.lean

